  "id": "COMPOUND:19297 - PROTEIN:279",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that (12S,13S)-12,13-Epoxylabda-8(17),14-Dien-19-Oic Acid is a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately interact with High affinity cationic amino acid transporter 1. This relationship is supported by the shared target of NCI-H2171, which is a known target of several compounds, including 2-(4-methoxyphenyl)-7-[(2S,3R,4S,5S,6R)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[[(2S,3R,4S,5R)-3,4,5-trihydroxyoxan-2-yl]oxymethyl]oxan-2-yl]oxychromen-4-one, 6,8-Dihydroxy-3-Methylisocoumarin, and kaempferol 3-O-(6\"-O-feruloyl)-glucoside. These compounds likely act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the transporter's function or activity, which is consistent with the observed target relationship. The integration of these pathways highlights the transporter's role as a potential mediator in the biological effects of these compounds, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
